WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:03.280
Hey Youtubers, it's Charlie

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:05.620
So this is going to be my Walking Dead Episode 12 video

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.900
The first look inside the Alexandria Safe Zone

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:11.760
We also got to meet a couple people that were right out of the comics

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:14.160
so I'll try to explain them in the most non-spoilery way possible

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:17.685
So just careful for spoilers as I start to explain who these people are

00:00:18.103 --> 00:00:18.903
So here we go

00:00:18.903 --> 00:00:23.980
Deanna first.  She is a gender-bent version of Douglas Monroe from the comics 

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:27.177
and aside from the gender swapping, she's pretty much the same as she is in the comics

00:00:27.177 --> 00:00:31.326
She's an Ohio representative, she's a politician, so definitely don't trust her

00:00:31.326 --> 00:00:36.900
In the comics Douglas did have a son named Spencer, but on the show Deanna's son's name is Aiden

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:40.200
So Aiden might be a little bit like Spencer in the comics at least in tone

00:00:40.443 --> 00:00:42.063
like the characters are both douchebags

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:45.640
but it seems like Aiden's character is gonna be much more aggressive.

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:48.020
Then we have Jessi here, also right out of the comics, 

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:48.980
she has a son named Ron

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:50.380
On the show she has two sons,

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.980
I don't want to talk about her husband in the comics cause it's a little spoilery, and

00:00:53.985 --> 00:00:57.312
they kind of teed it up with Rick walking by their porch

00:00:57.312 --> 00:01:00.135
but if your ears pricked up whenever she and Rick were sharing moments

00:01:00.135 --> 00:01:00.940
then you're on the right track

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:06.199
In general, it seems like the show is going to be pretty faithful to the Safe Zone of the comics, with a few minor changes

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:08.015
Not quite as many characters

00:01:08.015 --> 00:01:11.755
If you have read the comics, and you want to talk about that stuff, just please use spoiler tags

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:13.140
So here we go, top five moments:

00:01:13.148 --> 00:01:15.094
Number 5 - Welcome to the Safe Zone

00:01:15.094 --> 00:01:17.545
This episode is one of my favorites so far this season

00:01:17.545 --> 00:01:20.460
And for very different reasons than I usually get excited about episodes

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:25.798
Usually Walking Dead is all about the gore, all about big zombie kills, really awesome effect sequences

00:01:25.798 --> 00:01:29.760
but this episode was all about the group stepping into this alternate dimension 

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:32.080
where they just couldn't fathom what was going on

00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:34.152
because it looked so weird

00:01:34.152 --> 00:01:38.341
it's like they all walk in and they're looking around going "What the HELL is going on here?"

00:01:38.341 --> 00:01:43.500
When I first graduated from college, I moved into a neighborhood kind of like that, and I had the exact same reaction.

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:46.871
I was like, "what is going on? These people look like aliens."

00:01:46.871 --> 00:01:50.604
That being said, I do think that most of the members of the group have their shit together.

00:01:50.654 --> 00:01:54.174
Carol totally isn't drinking the Kool-Aid, Rick knows what's up

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:57.940
I mean he puts that uniform on, but that doesn't mean that he's going to stop being careful

00:01:58.220 --> 00:02:03.520
I think the only one from start to finish that just refuses to accept their new reality is Daryl.

00:02:03.522 --> 00:02:05.740
Moving on to Number 4 - say good-bye to Rick's beard!

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:07.360
May you rest in peace

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:12.060
This was so funny.  I mean, Andrew Lincoln had been walking around in real life without a beard for a long time

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:15.015
so I think we all felt like, yeah, eventually they're going to trim it

00:02:15.439 --> 00:02:17.599
It got so ridiculously long, too

00:02:17.599 --> 00:02:23.153
The minute Aaron showed up, clean shaven, you're like, okay, yeah, clearly he is from a place where they own razors.

00:02:23.153 --> 00:02:24.733
The beard is not long for this world.

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:28.075
How many years, though did it take off of Rick's life when he cut that beard off?

00:02:28.075 --> 00:02:31.699
He's not an old man, but with that beard, he definitely looked like one.

00:02:31.873 --> 00:02:33.873
It's like he de-aged by 10 years 

00:02:33.873 --> 00:02:34.600
the minute he shaved

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:40.571
and how convenient that Alexandra Breckenridge's Jessi character showed up right as he was finishing, no shirt on

00:02:40.571 --> 00:02:42.567
Clearly there's going to be some shenanigans going on there eventually

00:02:42.567 --> 00:02:46.866
Whenever they cast Alexandra Breckenridge, they made a pretty big deal about it.  She's one of the few

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:50.232
characters, I mean, there's a bunch of new characters at the Safe Zone, but she's one of the few that they made

00:02:50.232 --> 00:02:54.060
a big deal about publicizing, so obviously they're going to focus a lot more on her

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:55.447
in terms of all these new people.

00:02:55.447 --> 00:02:59.707
That just means that she's going to have a lot more scenes with the group than the other new members of the Safe Zone

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:04.820
I think we're going to be at the Safe Zone for the rest of the season, and so we will have time to meet all those other characters,

00:03:04.821 --> 00:03:07.201
but I just feel like they're going to focus more on Jessi.

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:10.680
Moving on to Number 3 - Carl meets all the children

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:14.700
I like the way they have parallels between the group members in the way they experience the Safe Zone

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:20.000
So Carl is like the kid version of Daryl.  Completely cannot figure out how to assimilate.

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:23.080
There is the Enid character, clearly he's going to form a bond with her

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:25.451
I'm kind of interested to see what's going on there

00:03:25.451 --> 00:03:27.601
She could wind up being like a Clementine character

00:03:27.601 --> 00:03:28.524
from the video game

00:03:28.524 --> 00:03:32.914
I don't think she is Clementine, or it could go nowhere, but I'm more inclined to think

00:03:32.914 --> 00:03:35.420
that based on the amount of time they spent setting her character up

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:38.260
teasing that something was going to happen between her and Carl

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:39.500
that they will pursue that

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:46.220
Definitely something going on with Rich-onne, with this new Jessi character and Rick, and now Carl has this new Enid character

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:48.320
Just a lot of new friendships that are going to be born

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:56.060
Think about it this way, too, a lot of times, if the  Walking Dead ends up really liking an actor, if their performance ends up being way better than they originally thought it would be

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:59.420
sometimes they'll turn them into cast regulars in future seasons

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:05.420
Robert Kirkman has said a number of times, though, that this season will be much more faithful to the comics

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:08.480
So, just regardless, look forward to a lots of comic book things

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:12.780
Moving on to Number 2 - The Survivors clash with life at the Safe Zone

00:04:13.089 --> 00:04:20.089
So everyone acts out just a little bit in their own way.  Carl and Rick have that weird moment where they get super cranked up to kill walkers together

00:04:20.089 --> 00:04:21.897
I guess it's like their version of catch

00:04:21.897 --> 00:04:23.080
Their version of playing catch in the backyard.

00:04:23.080 --> 00:04:27.000
And they you have Glenn, Tara, and Noah, clashing with Aiden's group

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:31.420
Clearly Aiden is off his rocker.  They're all just having a hard time assimilating.

00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:34.000
I mean Daryl is just the best visible example of that.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:38.994
It's like taking a wild dog and putting it in a house, like, it will just keep freaking out til it adjusts.

00:04:38.994 --> 00:04:40.980
Or til you let it back outside.

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:47.628
And finally, my number one moment - Rick says that if it doesn't work out, don't worry, we'll just take the place.

00:04:47.628 --> 00:04:49.213
The way he said that too, such a great delivery

00:04:49.349 --> 00:04:49.989
So casual

00:04:49.989 --> 00:04:52.900
Like, don't worry, We'll just take it, no big deal.

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:58.120
He and Carol are so funny, like it's like they're wearing these weird clothes, now, like Carol's dressed like a housewife

00:04:58.120 --> 00:05:02.133
He's dressed like he used to as a sheriff, but underneath they're not taking any bullshit.

00:05:02.133 --> 00:05:07.001
I would say of all the camera performances, Carol's was my favorite, though.  Everyone else seemed so earnest.

00:05:07.001 --> 00:05:10.281
Like Rick was honest, he's like "Close your gates, don't trust anyone"

00:05:10.780 --> 00:05:15.140
Carol, though, was like "OH, I'm just a den mother, I love working with other people."

00:05:15.140 --> 00:05:17.800
"Do you have any jobs in the community? Do you have a Junior League?

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:19.720
Any organizations that I can help?"

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:23.911
Just the way her face looked while she was saying that seemed so earnest and so funny.

00:05:24.140 --> 00:05:25.580
I just wanted to laugh so hard.

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:28.200
Clearly she is just playing this politician.

00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:31.718
And that's another thing, too.  What is going on with Deanna?

00:05:31.718 --> 00:05:34.520
If she's a politician, that means that she lies for a living.

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:38.520
And if she's good enough to win re-election, that means she's really good at manipulating people.

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:44.670
I think just right now, since she's just met these people, what she's doing is she senses that they're really tough

00:05:44.914 --> 00:05:46.834
so she's keeping them close.

00:05:46.834 --> 00:05:48.420
Like she's trying to make friends with them right away.

00:05:48.420 --> 00:05:51.791
If you were to meet someone who you sensed was more powerful than you, 

00:05:51.791 --> 00:05:56.320
you'd have a much easier time if you befriended them rather than turn them into an immediate enemy.

00:05:56.320 --> 00:06:03.030
Doesn't that just feel like a politician thing to do?  Like if you saw an opponent that you thought might be able to beat you in a future election

00:06:03.030 --> 00:06:04.747
You would try to turn them into an ally.

00:06:04.747 --> 00:06:08.200
rather than keep them from becoming an enemy or potential threat in the future

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:11.569
But let me know though, of all the things that they teased in the episode, 

00:06:11.569 --> 00:06:17.418
like potential future conflicts with certain people, especially with Jessi's weirdo husband smoking creepily on the porch

00:06:17.418 --> 00:06:19.225
what are you most excited about?

00:06:19.225 --> 00:06:23.892
One of the fun things I'm really looking forward to is just seeing Glenn beat the shit out of Aiden

00:06:24.017 --> 00:06:24.517
again

00:06:24.517 --> 00:06:28.075
there's no way he's going to let that go.  Aiden is totally going to challenge him again at some point.

00:06:28.075 --> 00:06:31.140
I already mentioned most of the comic book easter eggs I saw,

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:34.820
like all the people that they pulled straight off the page, but if you saw any that I didn't mention, 

00:06:34.991 --> 00:06:36.091
just list them in the comments below.

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:44.420
I think one of the things that we need to look out for is who took Rick's gun, what's going to happen with the other members of the community that we haven't met yet

00:06:44.860 --> 00:06:48.700
and what is Aiden going to do to get revenge on Glenn?

00:06:48.704 --> 00:06:52.940
Based on what they put in the teaser for the next episode, I think we're going to learn a lot more about Deanna

00:06:52.940 --> 00:06:59.180
next week.  So, I think we'll find a little bit more about what's going on inside her head.  What her grand plan is for the survivors.

00:06:59.180 --> 00:07:04.860
And remember the producers and Robert Kirkman have said that we're going to meet a villain this season that's just as bad as the governor

00:07:05.246 --> 00:07:06.206
and the people at Terminus.

00:07:06.460 --> 00:07:10.240
Don't you just wonder if it's someone that we met in this episode?  Because I don't think it's going to be Negan.  

00:07:10.380 --> 00:07:12.780
I think he's still a little ways off.

